/**
 * @page topic_client_keepalive Connection Keepalive
 * @ingroup module_client
 * @brief Liveness probes and timeout handling for an established connection.
 *
 * Keepalive uses the shared ACIP control path. It sends `acip_send_ping()` on
 * the connection transport and records matching pong packets through protocol
 * handlers. It does not write directly to a client socket.
 *
 * @section client_keepalive_timeouts Deadlines
 *
 * Connection establishment, partial-packet, idle, and cancellation deadlines
 * belong to the connection/backend. Keepalive observes those states and
 * requests shutdown or reconnect when the session is no longer usable; it must
 * not add an independent blocking receive loop.
 *
 * @section client_keepalive_shutdown Shutdown
 *
 * A timeout stops media producers first, requests the connection worker to stop,
 * and lets the normal closing/closed callbacks release state. Reconnect starts a
 * fresh transport and handshake rather than reusing a stale timer or queue.
 *
 * @see topic_client_connection
 * @see topic_network
 */
